const buildInterpretations={
 'graph-database-models':'Type and source filtering retain outgoing dependency facts; projecting target IDs answers which resources this asset directly requires.',
 'graph-database-identity':'The structured source/key pair keeps different plants separate, while duplicate detection exposes repeated identity records for an explicit reconciliation policy.',
 'graph-pattern-matching':'Each expansion continues the same binding. The final distinct technician IDs therefore come from inspections attached to the requested asset.',
 'graph-filtering-aggregation':'The result counts distinct closed Inspection identities within each asset, so repeated relationships cannot inflate the count.',
 'graph-optional-patterns':'Optional extension preserves every registered asset. Counting only non-null distinct inspection IDs turns a missing qualifying match into a visible zero.',
 'graph-traversal-cycles':'The visited set stops repeated expansion through the cycle, while the depth record identifies the explicitly bounded reachable set.',
 'graph-shortest-paths':'When a cheaper route is found, its accumulated cost replaces the earlier cost for that destination. This workshop requires nonnegative edge times. The final lookup keeps an unreachable destination distinct from the start, whose travel cost is zero.',
 'graph-constraints-indexes':'Repeated usable IDs and missing usable IDs are independent violations. Keeping both results prevents uniqueness from being mistaken for complete key validity.',
 'graph-safe-updates':'Explicit approval and a matching snapshot revision identify requests eligible for the next transaction stage; this preflight result is not evidence of a committed write.',
 'graph-imports':'Classification separates new resolvable relationships from replays and rejected rows. The admission list names staged work while the intermediate audit retains reasons for omission.',
 'graph-query-performance':'The pair compares specified candidate-check counts over the same typed edges and distinct starts. It excludes index construction and does not predict database latency.',
 'graph-rdf-sparql':'The resource projection preserves RDF object categories, then predicate and target matching yield distinct subject resources rather than literal lookalikes.',
 'graph-provenance':'Source and time filters select eligible claim evidence without erasing conflicting statements or asserting that the surviving sources must be correct.',
 'graph-ml-retrieval':'Scope is applied before dependency expansion. Document availability then excludes future evidence while the permitted route structure excludes cross-tenant detours.'
};
